Subject: Render the on-screen keyboard on the OVERLAY layer

Squeekboard requests the layer-shell TOP layer, which wlroots-based
compositors stack *below* fullscreen surfaces. In a fullscreen kiosk
(e.g. Chromium/Electron under labwc) the keyboard is therefore never
visible, even though it initialises and receives input-method events.

Moving the panel to the OVERLAY layer stacks it above fullscreen
surfaces, which is the desired behaviour for kiosk use.

--- a/src/panel.c
+++ b/src/panel.c
@@ -79,7 +79,7 @@
             "anchor", ZWLR_LAYER_SURFACE_V1_ANCHOR_BOTTOM
             | ZWLR_LAYER_SURFACE_V1_ANCHOR_LEFT
             | ZWLR_LAYER_SURFACE_V1_ANCHOR_RIGHT,
-            "layer", ZWLR_LAYER_SHELL_V1_LAYER_TOP,
+            "layer", ZWLR_LAYER_SHELL_V1_LAYER_OVERLAY,
             "kbd-interactivity", FALSE,
             "exclusive-zone", height,
             "namespace", "osk",
